Many adults never learned to swim as children. Swimming schools report that the number of adult beginners has doubled in the last five years. Most are aged between thirty and fifty. A typical course lasts eight weeks and costs sixty pounds. Instructors say that the biggest problem is fear of water, not lack of fitness, so lessons start in shallow water and move to deeper pools only after students feel confident.', 'VALID');
