A. Tea was first drunk in China more than two thousand years ago, probably as a medicine. By the eighth century it was a popular drink across the country, and special tea houses opened in the cities.

B. Traders brought tea to Europe in the seventeenth century. At first it was so expensive that only rich families could buy it. Prices fell when merchants began to grow tea in India in the nineteenth century.

C. Today tea is the second most drunk liquid in the world, after water. The average person in Turkey drinks more than three kilograms of tea leaves a year, which is more than in any other country.', 'VALID');
