A. More people now work from home at least one day a week. Employers say this saves money on office space, and workers say it saves time on the journey to work.

B. There are problems too. Some people find it hard to stop working in the evening, and others miss talking to colleagues. Companies therefore ask staff to keep regular hours and to meet in the office once a week.

C. Experts expect the pattern to continue, because both workers and companies see clear advantages.', 'VALID');
